            <ArticleTitle>[Symptomatic bladder calculi: diagnostic and therapeutic aspects].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>93-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors report the case of a 50 years old woman who consulted with bilateral lumbar pain and urinary infections. Intravenous Urography (IVU) showed bilateral renal and bladder stones. Treatment was by upper polary nephrectomy in the left kidney. Removing all urinary and bladder stone. We then the removed surgically renal stones in the right kidney. Using this case as an we discuss the diagnosis and therapeutic aspects of the hydrocalyx.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
